atlas institutional-namespaces

architecture institutional-namespaces
  canonical_name InstitutionalNamespaces
  owns RootNamespace
  consumes AddressExpr
  consumes PackState
  publishes RootNamespace
  publishes PopulationState
  family institutional
  domain Institution / AddressPlane namespaces
  layer forwarding
  semantic_question What is the stable address of this estate, and is that address backed by state today?
  purpose Give every root product and delegated estate one AddressPlane namespace so the atlas can descend from the engine root into a specific relationship, managed client, capability or work item without a bespoke lookup per product.
  maturity architectural
  node_types Namespace
  node_types PopulationState
  edge_types descends_from
  edge_types populated_by
  invariant every root namespace declares one population state from REAL, SEEDED or DECLARED
  invariant DECLARED means the namespace exists and nothing populates it; it is never rendered as an existing estate
  invariant a namespace is populated by packs or existing state, never by this file
  invariant an estate's namespace is stable across repopulation so addresses survive a rebuild of the state beneath them
  invariant the delegated parent declares its leadership tuple -- estate, role, scope, permission and object -- so a vertical organ asks who leads a delegated estate by reading the contract rather than by comparing five compiled strings
  invariant a delegated parent declares its whole leadership tuple or none of it; a half-declared leadership is two authority sources disagreeing, and the generator refuses it
  forbidden_inference a delegated vertical's storage carrying a tenant's name -> that tenant being the type of every delegated estate (the rows were always estate-aware; only the table names were not)
  forbidden_inference a DECLARED namespace -> an empty estate that may be discarded
  forbidden_inference a SEEDED namespace -> a materialized product
  interacts address-plane
  interacts institutional-root
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/contracts.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreAtlas/bonfyre-atlas compile-contracts institutions --check-generated proves the institutional JSON and C header agree with this namespace contract without granting access
  source_lineage disk census 2026-08-26

namespace bonfyre
  population REAL
  detail Engine and product substrate. Root of every namespace below.

namespace bonfyre/internal
  population REAL
  populated_by .bonfyre/run8/state.sqlite3
  populated_by packs/run-history
  populated_by packs/system-upgrades
  detail Bonfyre operating itself. Run8 is the native operating system for building Bonfyre with Bonfyre, not a setup phase that ends.

namespace bonfyre/internal/run8/work
  population REAL
  detail 136 work_items at census
namespace bonfyre/internal/run8/epochs
  population REAL
  detail 192 epochs at census
namespace bonfyre/internal/run8/receipts
  population REAL
  detail 192 receipts at census, 125 claude and 67 codex
namespace bonfyre/internal/run8/proof
  population REAL
  detail 507 anti_amnesia records at census
namespace bonfyre/internal/run8/providers
  population REAL
  detail 2 provider_state rows at census
namespace bonfyre/internal/run8/mesh
  population REAL
  detail 118 mesh_events and 112 mesh_delivery rows at census

namespace bonfyre/personal
  population REAL
  populated_by tools/food_offer_observations.py
  populated_by tools/housing_*.py
  populated_by .bonfyre/run8-r2c/*/epochs/*/physical-realization-food/
  detail Private product. Owner-scoped today, household-scoped later, without copying the business hierarchy into it.
namespace bonfyre/personal/food
  population REAL
namespace bonfyre/personal/housing
  population REAL
namespace bonfyre/personal/external
  population DECLARED
  detail Observed institutions, accounts, memberships and eventual effect rails. Reserved deliberately; public observation, personal relationship and realization are three different things.

namespace bonfyre/habitat
  population SEEDED
  populated_by packs/habitat-human-factors
  detail Standalone social and spatial experiment. Its product language is person, group, space, presence, invite; not client, tenant, invoice.

namespace bonfyre/ventures
  population REAL
  populated_by packs/utd-vdc
  populated_by packs/acm-queue
  populated_by packs/tarbell
  populated_by packs/institutional-opportunities
  populated_by packs/adjacent-opportunities
  populated_by packs/technical-institutions
  detail Bonfyre's own future-facing institutional estate. Reachability is determined against proof, work and authority rather than by declaring an opportunity available.

namespace bonfyre/ventures/fleming-equity-group
  population SEEDED
  populated_by packs/fleming-equity-group
  detail A DFW commercial-property relationship estate. The seed contains source-bound observations, a non-actionable flyer fixture and work; it does not establish a client agreement, title, licensing, buyer appetite or an opportunity's reachability.

namespace bonfyre/collaborations
  population DECLARED
  detail Direct project collaborations such as Bernstein, DeepEval, AgentGuard, Agent Inspect, Deputy, ChainWeaver. Namespace established without state. To be derived from actual issue, PR and maintainer evidence, never by promoting a Partner Commons profile into a fake relationship.

namespace bonfyre/partner-commons
  population REAL
  detail Method and realization bank. Not an integration list and not a relationship list.

namespace bonfyre/delegated
  population REAL
  detail Estates Bonfyre delegates to an operating business that holds its own relationships, clients and users.

namespace upper90
  population REAL
  populated_by packs/upper90
  parent bonfyre
  delegated_parent true
  leadership_role upper90-leadership
  leadership_permission upper90:private-access
  leadership_object upper90-private-workspace
  detail First complete delegated vertical. Reference implementation of institutional delegation.
  detail The parent link is declared rather than inferred: upper90 is a top-level
  detail namespace, not bonfyre/upper90, so nesting does not carry it. A bonfyre
  detail grant opens upper90 and everything upper90 manages; the reverse never holds.
  detail The leadership tuple is declared here because the vertical organ tested
  detail it as five separate string literals -- estate, role, scope, permission and
  detail object. That is institutional law living in an organ, so a second delegated
  detail parent would have required a code change rather than a contract line.
namespace upper90/relationships
  population REAL
namespace upper90/providers
  population REAL
namespace upper90/capabilities
  population REAL
namespace upper90/managed
  population REAL
namespace upper90/managed/jrss
  population REAL
  inherited_role jrss-internal-admin
namespace upper90/managed/ai-loss
  population REAL
  inherited_role ai-loss-admin
  # The pack carrying this product's grammar. Declared here so generic machinery
  # discovers a namespace's contracts rather than embedding the product's name in
  # a filename, a schema string or an import.
  product_pack packs/upper90/product-contract-ai-loss.yaff
namespace upper90/managed/leads
  population REAL
  inherited_role leads-demo-admin
  detail Held a live institution grant and an MCP institutional slice while this
  detail contract declared no namespace for it. Distinct from upper90/demo, which
  detail is the Leads Demo -- a DemoInstitution in world DEMO, not this estate.
namespace upper90/demo
  population SEEDED
  detail Leads Demo. A DemoInstitution in world DEMO, not a client with fake data.
namespace upper90/work
  population REAL

# Deep Ellum Night Grid -- the demo institution the authority lattice is tested
# against.
#
# Declared as its own root rather than under upper90 because it is not a client
# Upper90 manages; it is a separate institution that happens to execute in the
# DEMO world. Putting it under upper90/managed would have made every lattice
# assertion about it also an assertion about Upper90's ancestry, which is
# exactly the contortion the frontier warns against.
#
# Every persona below is synthetic. The venues, creators and sponsor are
# invented for this estate and are not observations of real Deep Ellum
# businesses. A real business may still enter through ForeignTwin with its own
# epistemic status; it never becomes one of these.

namespace nightgrid
  population SEEDED
  world DEMO
  demo_institution true
  detail Deep Ellum Night Grid. A DemoInstitution in world DEMO: synthetic members,
  detail real institutional mechanics. It exists to hold the intermediate authority
  detail states no real estate currently occupies -- one-institution read, write
  detail without finance, finance without admin, publication without member
  detail administration -- and to be one Matrix world projected across four
  detail territories rather than four demo sites.
  detail Cannot infer: a persona exercising a capability here -> that capability
  detail being authorized in a LIVE institution.
  detail Bound at nightgrid.aurekai.live with institution:nightgrid registered in
  detail matrix_institutions as a DemoInstitution in world DEMO. Five synthetic
  detail subjects are authored in CMS and projected by four surface patterns that
  detail read the one content type with different field sets, which is the whole
  detail demonstration: one Matrix world seen four lawful ways, not four datasets.
  detail Served at /tonight on all four territories rather than at a dedicated host:
  detail a separate nightgrid host would have needed its own certificate and would
  detail have proved the opposite thing, that the demo is a site rather than a
  detail projection. A reader can open two territories side by side and see one
  detail institution described two lawful ways.
namespace nightgrid/venues
  population SEEDED
namespace nightgrid/creators
  population SEEDED
namespace nightgrid/campaigns
  population SEEDED
namespace nightgrid/events
  population SEEDED
namespace nightgrid/safety
  population SEEDED

# The persona lattice. Each line is a role, the institutional rank it holds, and
# the capability class it is allowed to touch. The point of declaring it is that
# "a venue operator must not gain district admin" becomes a row a test can read
# rather than a sentence in a plan.
persona_lattice nightgrid
  persona organizer      admin  events,members,publication
  persona venue          write  merchant,offers,capacity
  persona creator        write  creator,deliverables
  persona sponsor        write  finance,campaign-budget
  persona editor         write  publication
  persona safety         write  safety,operations
  persona member         read   participation
  persona machine        read   machine-closure

# The institutional role lattice, ranked.
#
# read < write < admin was a strcmp ladder inside BonfyreAuth. A rank decides
# whether a held grant satisfies a required role, so the ordering is an
# authority policy, not a formatting detail -- and it was legible only by
# reading the comparison that used it.
institution_roles
  role read 0
  role write 1
  role admin 2
  forbidden_inference a higher rank -> authority over an estate the grant does not name
